course: dictionary
lesson: 16011
title: Variously: many names, many views
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Variously» means in different ways, or by different people at different times. When you see it, the writer is telling you that people do not all agree. «The old bridge is variously described as beautiful and dangerous.» Some people think it is beautiful, and others think it is dangerous.
explain: The word often comes before «described as», «called» or «known as». «The river is variously called the Blue River, the Silver Stream and the Long Water.» One river, three names. Ask yourself: did people use just one name?
explain: A quick check is to swap in the words «in different ways». In the bridge sentence, «The old bridge is in different ways described as beautiful and dangerous» still makes sense, so variously is the right word.
fact: «Variously» is an adverb, so it tells you how something is described or done.
fact: «Variously» means in different ways, or by different people at different times.
fact: It is a written, slightly formal word, so you will meet it more in books and news than in everyday talk.
fact: «Variously» is related to «various», which means several different kinds of something.
fact: Use «variously» when people use several names or descriptions for the same thing: «The hill is variously known as Pen Hill and Grey Top.»
exercise: «The fruit is variously described as sweet and sour.» What does variously show here? | *People describe it in different ways | It is hidden inside a tree | It is always sour | It is always sweet
exercise: Ella says variously means always. What does it actually mean? | Only once | Always the same | Very quickly | *In different ways, or by different people
exercise: Which word in «The hill is variously known as Pen Hill and Grey Top» shows that people use several names? | hill | Top | *variously | known
test: «The shop is variously described as cosy and cramped.» What does variously tell the reader? | *That people give different descriptions | That the shop is very large | That everyone agrees completely | That the shop is closed
test: Which phrase best matches the meaning of variously? | without any sound | in exactly the same way | *in different ways | very quickly
exam: Which best explains variously in «The lake is variously called Green Lake and Mirror Water»? | Always the same name | Only one person has ever seen it | Very cold water | *Several names, used by different people
